## E3_1_SpendBelowTheCap

E-3.1 reimburses "meal expenses ... up to" the cap, so a smaller spend is
reimbursed in full and the cap is not an allowance.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestE3_1_SpendBelowTheCap:
  output r content MealPerDiem.MealPerDiemForDay

scope TestE3_1_SpendBelowTheCap:
  definition r equals
    output of MealPerDiem.MealPerDiemForDay with {
      -- city_tier: ExpenseDefs.CityTier.Tier1
      -- client_billable: not_client_billable
      -- pre_approval: no_pre_approval
      -- incurred_on: |2025-06-10|
      -- meals_provided_free: 0
      -- meal_expense_incurred: $30.00
      -- on_critical_incident_response: false
    }
  assertion r.per_diem_cap = $75.00
  assertion r.reimbursable_amount = $30.00
```

