      -- incurred_on: |2025-06-10|
      -- meals_provided_free: 0
      -- meal_expense_incurred: $200.00
      -- on_critical_incident_response: false
    }
  assertion r.per_diem_cap = $60.00
```

## E3_2_SowAmountGovernsEvenWhenLower

E-3.2 first limb: where the statement of work specifies an amount, "the
applicable per diem is the amount specified" — the clause neither floors it at
the E-3.1 figure nor compares it to the 1.5x fallback.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestE3_2_SowAmountGovernsEvenWhenLower:
  output r content MealPerDiem.MealPerDiemForDay

scope TestE3_2_SowAmountGovernsEvenWhenLower:
  definition r equals
    output of MealPerDiem.MealPerDiemForDay with {
      -- city_tier: ExpenseDefs.CityTier.Tier1
      -- client_billable: client_billable_with_sow of $40.00
      -- pre_approval: no_pre_approval
      -- incurred_on: |2025-06-10|
      -- meals_provided_free: 0
      -- meal_expense_incurred: $200.00
      -- on_critical_incident_response: false
    }
  assertion r.per_diem_cap = $40.00
```

## E3_3_PreApprovedHigherAmountNotClientBillable

E-3.3 is an exception to E-3.1 as well as to E-3.2, so it must fire on travel
that is not Client-Billable at all. If the encoding had wrongly repeated E-3.2's
condition in the exception, this test would return £75.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestE3_3_PreApprovedHigherAmountNotClientBillable:
  output r content MealPerDiem.MealPerDiemForDay

scope TestE3_3_PreApprovedHigherAmountNotClientBillable:
  definition r equals
    output of MealPerDiem.MealPerDiemForDay with {
      -- city_tier: ExpenseDefs.CityTier.Tier1
      -- client_billable: not_client_billable
      -- pre_approval: pre_approval_for of $150.00
      -- incurred_on: |2025-06-10|
      -- meals_provided_free: 0
      -- meal_expense_incurred: $200.00
      -- on_critical_incident_response: false
    }
  assertion r.per_diem_cap = $150.00
  assertion r.reimbursable_amount = $150.00
```

## E3_3_PreApprovedHigherAmountDisplacesE3_2

E-3.3 defeats E-3.2 as well: £150 beats the £112.50 that E-3.2 would give.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestE3_3_PreApprovedHigherAmountDisplacesE3_2:
  output r content MealPerDiem.MealPerDiemForDay

scope TestE3_3_PreApprovedHigherAmountDisplacesE3_2:
  definition r equals
    output of MealPerDiem.MealPerDiemForDay with {
      -- city_tier: ExpenseDefs.CityTier.Tier1
      -- client_billable: client_billable_no_sow_amount
      -- pre_approval: pre_approval_for of $150.00
      -- incurred_on: |2025-06-10|
      -- meals_provided_free: 0
      -- meal_expense_incurred: $200.00
      -- on_critical_incident_response: false
    }
  assertion r.per_diem_cap = $150.00
```

## E3_3_PreApprovedAmountNotHigherThanE3_1

E-3.3 applies to a "specified **higher** amount". £60 is not higher than the
£75 E-3.1 gives, so the E-3.1 cap stands and a Pre-Approval cannot cut the per
diem down.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestE3_3_PreApprovedAmountNotHigherThanE3_1:
  output r content MealPerDiem.MealPerDiemForDay

scope TestE3_3_PreApprovedAmountNotHigherThanE3_1:
  definition r equals
    output of MealPerDiem.MealPerDiemForDay with {
      -- city_tier: ExpenseDefs.CityTier.Tier1
      -- client_billable: not_client_billable
      -- pre_approval: pre_approval_for of $60.00
      -- incurred_on: |2025-06-10|
      -- meals_provided_free: 0
      -- meal_expense_incurred: $200.00
      -- on_critical_incident_response: false
    }
  assertion r.per_diem_cap = $75.00
```

